<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN"
  "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  com.comms.thread-compile.plist -- TEMPLATE, not a ready-to-load plist.

  launchd cannot expand $HOME or resolve a checkout's own path, so the four
  double-underscore placeholders in the ProgramArguments/StandardOutPath/
  StandardErrorPath strings below are filled in by adapters/launchd/
  install.sh at copy time (same shape as adapters/discord/install.sh
  resolving $MIRROR from its own location before printing it): an absolute
  interpreter path (from `command -v python3`), this checkout's absolute
  path to scripts/comms_compile_threads.py, and two absolute log paths
  under ~/Library/Logs/comms. Do not `launchctl bootstrap` this file
  directly from the repo -- install.sh writes the filled-in copy to
  ~/Library/LaunchAgents first. NOTE: install.sh's substitution is a blind
  file-wide sed, so if you are reading this comment IN THE INSTALLED COPY
  rather than the checkout, these words have already been replaced by the
  real values below -- read the checked-out template for the placeholder
  names themselves.

  StartInterval (every 3600 s), not StartCalendarInterval. The calendar form
  was the design (18:00 check-in, 23:00 close) but on studio, 2026-08-25,
  two valid calendar slots (23:00 and 23:15) never fired while
  `launchctl kickstart` and a StartInterval timer both ran the job within
  seconds; launchd logged nothing. The compile is watermark-driven and
  idempotent (notes_written=0 when nothing changed), so an hourly interval
  is safe and the day's note simply refreshes through the evening. Revisit
  the calendar form only with a fresh proof that it fires on this fleet.

  No KeepAlive: unlike the Discord mirror's --follow loops, this job is a
  one-shot compile that exits when done. KeepAlive would restart it in a
  crash loop instead of waiting for the next scheduled minute.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.comms.thread-compile</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>__PYTHON3__</string>
    <string>__SCRIPT__</string>
  </array>
  <key>StartInterval</key>
  <integer>3600</integer>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>__STDOUT_LOG__</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>__STDERR_LOG__</string>
</dict>
</plist>
